- op: discuss  # 0794
  at: '2026-07-02T00:44:50Z'  # 0794
  by: agent  # 0794
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0794
  clock: 4  # 0794
  nonce: '0794'  # 0794
  message: "DONE (argparse) via dev 2e9611808f. Root cause was deeper than the filed 'cli.yaml mis-keys concept under decorator': the subprocess linker joins subcommand-string -> command-symbol BY NAME, and argparse subcommands are add_parser('name') string LITERALS + set_defaults(func=handler) — not symbols — so re-keying the YAML could never help (the analyzer emits no usage_contexts for the constructor either; verified: 0 concepts on an argparse fixture). Fix: made the linker itself argparse-aware — _scan_argparse_commands walks each Python file's AST, pairs add_parser/set_defaults by parser-var, resolves func= to its module symbol, and merges {subcommand: handler} into command_by_name. Behavioral evidence (full pipeline via the registered linker): a fixture with add_parser('serve')+set_defaults(func=cmd_serve) and subprocess.run(['myapp','serve']) now emits subprocess_calls -> cmd_serve (meta.subcommand='serve'); BEFORE = no edge (0 concept=command symbols). Non-resolvable forms skipped (dynamic name, lambda/absent func, unresolved handler). Requirement diagnostic now counts both sources (concept=command + argparse handlers) — the machine-checkable prerequisite the item asked for. hypergumbo's own argparse CLI (~20 subcommands) is now joinable (self-dogfood). 100% coverage on subprocess_cli.py. Fire's reflective surface deferred -> follow-up filed. awaits_bakeoff_validation: a DEEP cohort with real argparse CLIs should confirm correct joins + no false positives."  # 0794
